From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 02:13:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(direct_io): accept external dma-buf device mappings under
 CUDA 13.5 compat

Upstream base: local-inference-lab/vllm 19f2c20ed4d64ae22bd009ceacadd85e2a81e354 (after candidate-54 0799).

Rationale:
On TP3 profiles (SPARK_DS41F_DISPLAY_CARVEOUT_WEIGHTS=1), display_carveout.allocate() places vocabulary-sized tables (embed_tokens.weight, lm_head.weight, DSpark markov_w1.weight) in GB10 scanout dumb buffers (/dev/dri/card0) imported via cuImportExternalMemory + cuExternalMemoryGetMappedBuffer. When CUDA 13.5's forward-compatibility driver (cuda-compat-13-5 620.70.06 over a 580.178.04 host kernel driver) is active, querying an imported external dma-buf device pointer returns CU_MEMORYTYPE_HOST (1) from CU_POINTER_ATTRIBUTE_MEMORY_TYPE (despite CU_POINTER_ATTRIBUTE_HOST_POINTER failing with CUDA_ERROR_INVALID_VALUE and CU_POINTER_ATTRIBUTE_DEVICE_POINTER returning the device pointer) and base == 0 from cuMemGetAddressRange (while CU_POINTER_ATTRIBUTE_RANGE_START_ADDR and CU_POINTER_ATTRIBUTE_RANGE_SIZE return the exact non-zero base and buffer size). This caused direct_io/_cuda_range.h:device_range() to reject embed_tokens.weight with "RuntimeError: batch destination exceeds CUDA device allocation" during DirectWeightSession.flush().

Changes:
- Update direct_io/_cuda_range.h (is_device_only_mapping, device_range) to accept CUDA mappings whose CU_POINTER_ATTRIBUTE_MEMORY_TYPE is CU_MEMORYTYPE_HOST only when CU_POINTER_ATTRIBUTE_HOST_POINTER fails (excluding all pinned/registered host memory) and CU_POINTER_ATTRIBUTE_DEVICE_POINTER equals the pointer, resolving base == 0 from cuMemGetAddressRange via CU_POINTER_ATTRIBUTE_RANGE_START_ADDR when CU_POINTER_ATTRIBUTE_RANGE_SIZE matches size.
- Add test_external_dmabuf_carveout_loads_and_rejects_out_of_bounds in tests/model_executor/model_loader/test_direct_loader_cuda.py verifying DirectWeightSession loading into a display_carveout buffer alongside out-of-bounds and pinned-host rejections.

Quality implications:
None. Weight values, dtypes, and copy semantics are unchanged; host buffers and out-of-bounds device ranges remain rejected before any I/O runs.

Tests:
- pytest tests/model_executor/model_loader/test_direct_loader.py tests/model_executor/model_loader/test_direct_loader_cuda.py tests/v1/worker/test_display_carveout.py under both host libcuda 580.178.04 (13000) and cuda-compat-13-5 libcuda 620.70.06 (13050).

Upstream status: spark-ds41f local candidate patch.
